WEBVTT

00:01:00.412 --> 00:01:03.454
It was thick with a churning,
humming plasma.

00:01:03.787 --> 00:01:05.454
It was hot and dense.

00:01:05.788 --> 00:01:06.996
It was loud.

00:01:07.413 --> 00:01:09.329
But it was also expanding.

00:01:09.371 --> 00:01:13.163
Over time, the fire dissipated
and space cooled.

00:01:13.496 --> 00:01:16.579
Clouds of gas pulled together
by their own gravity

00:01:16.621 --> 00:01:20.746
formed stars and galaxies
and planets and us.

00:01:21.454 --> 00:01:22.621
And one day,

00:01:22.663 --> 00:01:26.329
astronomers using a microwave
receiver detected a bit of static

00:01:26.371 --> 00:01:28.829
coming from every direction in the sky,

00:01:28.871 --> 00:01:32.371
the leftover radiation
from that primordial fire.